From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quill <siinspam@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 23:01:50 +0000
Subject: feat(nako): Bitwarden headless unlock and passkey sign-in

vault.bitwarden.master_password_command names an argv whose stdout is the
master password, so cron and other prompt-less sessions can fill saved
logins and mint TOTP codes the way a 1Password service token already
allows. vault.bitwarden.allowed_origins limits which logins are offered,
and appdata_dir points bw at a dedicated data directory.

browser_vault action=passkey loads a login's Bitwarden passkeys into a CDP
virtual authenticator on the sign-in tab (https page on the passkey's rp id
only). A watcher removes the authenticator after one sign-in or two minutes
and writes the advanced sign count back to the vault. Keys travel over the
supervisor socket and never appear in a result; list shows passkey_rp_ids.

Co-authored-by: Nako <nako@quill.moe>

